cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this toolkit or its results, please cite the master's thesis it is part of (preferred citation below)."
title: "5LTEP-L1 · Recife instance: 5L-TEP Layer 1 Structural Contracts Toolkit"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of Layer 1 (Structural Contracts) of the Five-Layer
  Trust Engineering Pyramid (5L-TEP, SOFTENG 2026) for open government data: a
  survey of every dataset of a CKAN portal on a schema maturity scale (from no
  dictionary to a machine-verifiable Table Schema), readers for the dictionaries
  portals publish (CSV, JSON, XML, XLSX, resource descriptions and PDF, the last
  through deterministic extraction, a local LLM and human review, with the
  published file's header as the oracle), streaming validation of every file
  against its declared schema with the Frictionless Table Schema, schema drift
  issues, and documentation findings. One value (the portal URL) adapts it to
  another CKAN portal. Part of the master's thesis cited below.
